\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Literature context of this release's 5$\sigma $ trigger thresholds, in total power (\S  \ref  {sec:background}). \emph  {(a)}\nobreakspace  {}EIRP against distance. Blue: this survey, deepest window per star (88{} stars, 1.30--39.63\,pc; filled: that window is Class A, drift-resolved; open: Class B, unresolved excess); orange: \citet  {Enriquez2017}; aqua: \citet  {Margot2023}; violet: \citet  {Mason2024}; left-edge ticks: deepest per-target limits of \citet  {Price2020}. Grey dotted: EIRP $\propto d^{2}$ at constant received flux, a guide not a fit. Green dashed: an Arecibo-like planetary radar, a technological power scale, not a model. \emph  {(b)}\nobreakspace  {}Native channel width against observing frequency for every searched window of this survey (filled Class A, open Class B) and for the four literature programmes (coloured segments): native resolutions differ by ${\sim }10^{7}$ between the Hz-resolution radio surveys and ALMA's correlator channels. All values are nominal trigger thresholds, and conventions differ among these surveys: context, not a ranking (in-panel note).}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:context}{{1}{3}{Literature context of this release's 5$\sigma $ trigger thresholds, in total power (\S \ref {sec:background}). \emph {(a)}~EIRP against distance. Blue: this survey, deepest window per star (\NStars {} stars, \DistMin --\DistMax \,pc; filled: that window is Class A, drift-resolved; open: Class B, unresolved excess); orange: \citet {Enriquez2017}; aqua: \citet {Margot2023}; violet: \citet {Mason2024}; left-edge ticks: deepest per-target limits of \citet {Price2020}. Grey dotted: EIRP $\propto d^{2}$ at constant received flux, a guide not a fit. Green dashed: an Arecibo-like planetary radar, a technological power scale, not a model. \emph {(b)}~Native channel width against observing frequency for every searched window of this survey (filled Class A, open Class B) and for the four literature programmes (coloured segments): native resolutions differ by ${\sim }10^{7}$ between the Hz-resolution radio surveys and ALMA's correlator channels. All values are nominal trigger thresholds, and conventions differ among these surveys: context, not a ranking (in-panel note)}{figure.1}{}}
