\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces What this survey sampled in frequency. Each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance, coloured by nominal EIRP$_{5\sigma }$, with line weight distinguishing the drift-resolved (Class A) from the unresolved-excess (Class B) channelisation; the upper panel counts systems per gigahertz of sky frequency. The narrow, clustered, repeatedly revisited coverage this shows -- 33{} islands concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, summed window bandwidth $7.6\times $ the union -- is what the in-band transmitter fractions of \S  \ref  {sec:discussion} condition on (Scope of the constraints, \S  \ref  {sec:method}). Thresholds are nominal in the sense of \S  \ref  {sec:method}.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:waterfall}{{2}{5}{What this survey sampled in frequency. Each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance, coloured by nominal EIRP$_{5\sigma }$, with line weight distinguishing the drift-resolved (Class A) from the unresolved-excess (Class B) channelisation; the upper panel counts systems per gigahertz of sky frequency. The narrow, clustered, repeatedly revisited coverage this shows -- \UnionIntervals {} islands concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, summed window bandwidth $7.6\times $ the union -- is what the in-band transmitter fractions of \S \ref {sec:discussion} condition on (Scope of the constraints, \S \ref {sec:method}). Thresholds are nominal in the sense of \S \ref {sec:method}}{figure.2}{}}
