\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces What the pipeline recovers, for the best-calibrated fine-channel configuration, against injected amplitude and drift fraction $f_{\rm  drift}$ (injected drift as a fraction of the searched ceiling). Carriers with $f_{\rm  drift}\leq 0.25$ show zero through-pipeline recovery at every amplitude -- a measured property of the through-pipeline path, distinct from the coarse-window criterion artefact withdrawn in \S  \ref  {sec:ancillary}: post-baseline injection (\S  \ref  {sec:dwell}) recovers near-static carriers, so the loss originates in the full path, not in the search statistic, and the searched-class completeness quotes below apply to the drifting class only. Carriers with $f_{\rm  drift}\geq 0.5$ recover progressively, from 42--83{} per cent between $5\sigma $ and $10\sigma $. Trial-level records were not retained for this campaign, so surviving fractions pool grid phase, sub-channel placement and the three drifting rows: the figure is drawn as discrete cells, not an interpolated surface, each column's hatched rows sharing one pooled measurement ($n=24$ per amplitude) rather than fifteen independent ones. Intervals are binomial Wilson 68 per cent; absorbed rows are measured zeros.}}{10}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:compsurface}{{4}{10}{What the pipeline recovers, for the best-calibrated fine-channel configuration, against injected amplitude and drift fraction $f_{\rm drift}$ (injected drift as a fraction of the searched ceiling). Carriers with $f_{\rm drift}\leq 0.25$ show zero through-pipeline recovery at every amplitude -- a measured property of the through-pipeline path, distinct from the coarse-window criterion artefact withdrawn in \S \ref {sec:ancillary}: post-baseline injection (\S \ref {sec:dwell}) recovers near-static carriers, so the loss originates in the full path, not in the search statistic, and the searched-class completeness quotes below apply to the drifting class only. Carriers with $f_{\rm drift}\geq 0.5$ recover progressively, from \RecThresh --\RecTwice {} per cent between $5\sigma $ and $10\sigma $. Trial-level records were not retained for this campaign, so surviving fractions pool grid phase, sub-channel placement and the three drifting rows: the figure is drawn as discrete cells, not an interpolated surface, each column's hatched rows sharing one pooled measurement ($n=24$ per amplitude) rather than fifteen independent ones. Intervals are binomial Wilson 68 per cent; absorbed rows are measured zeros}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {4.5}Dwell-fraction completeness}{10}{subsection.4.5}\protected@file@percent }
