\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The survey as frozen for this release, and the paper's headline numbers in one place. Every count quoted in this paper reconciles with this table; subset numbers are identified as such where used. Thresholds are nominal (boxed rule, \S  \ref  {sec:method}). The fine- and coarse-class recovery entries are not parallel measurements: the first is a threshold-completeness experiment, the second a dwell experiment at higher per-integration amplitude (\S  \ref  {sec:dwell}). The occurrence-rate formalism is a methodological demonstration (\S  \ref  {sec:null}, Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:population}) and is deliberately absent from these headline numbers.}}{12}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
