\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The four windows containing a stage-1 statistical flag and the evidence dispositioning each. $T_\star $ is the search statistic at the stellar position (Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {eq:tstar}), `ring max' the largest of that window's 512{} control statistics. $\Delta \nu $ and $\Delta v$ are the same offset of the crossing from the nearest of the eight masked species' catalogued transitions, in frequency and in velocity, topocentric; the $\pm 50$\,km\,s$^{-1}$ mask applies in the stellar frame after the conversion chain of Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:conventions}. Its application to these four windows is a \emph  {developmental} disposition -- the width was fixed after inspecting the $\beta $\nobreakspace  {}Pic crossings it must exclude -- whereas the same rule, now frozen, is the \emph  {confirmatory} criterion for the remaining datasets (\S  \ref  {sec:validation}). No disposition rests on a single test; the HD\nobreakspace  {}48370 row is the limiting case -- a near-tie of rank ($27.10$ against $26.83$) dispositioned by velocity coincidence with independently published emission (\S  \ref  {sec:technosearch}).}}{14}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:flagged}{{7}{14}{The four windows containing a stage-1 statistical flag and the evidence dispositioning each. $T_\star $ is the search statistic at the stellar position (Eq.~\ref {eq:tstar}), `ring max' the largest of that window's \NCtrl {} control statistics. $\Delta \nu $ and $\Delta v$ are the same offset of the crossing from the nearest of the eight masked species' catalogued transitions, in frequency and in velocity, topocentric; the $\pm 50$\,km\,s$^{-1}$ mask applies in the stellar frame after the conversion chain of Appendix~\ref {app:conventions}. Its application to these four windows is a \emph {developmental} disposition -- the width was fixed after inspecting the $\beta $~Pic crossings it must exclude -- whereas the same rule, now frozen, is the \emph {confirmatory} criterion for the remaining datasets (\S \ref {sec:validation}). No disposition rests on a single test; the HD~48370 row is the limiting case -- a near-tie of rank ($27.10$ against $26.83$) dispositioned by velocity coincidence with independently published emission (\S \ref {sec:technosearch})}{table.7}{}}
